<title>CANADA: DBRS puts Gulf Canada debt under review.</title>
<headline>DBRS puts Gulf Canada debt under review.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Bond Rating Service Ltd said on Wednesday it was placing its debt ratings for Gulf Canada Resources Ltd under review following Gulf's announcement of a C$972-million takeover bid for Britain's Clyde Petroleum Plc.</p>
<p>DBRS said current ratings for Gulf Canada included:</p>
<p>- BB (high) with a stable trend for long-term unsecured senior notes;</p>
<p>- B (high) with a stable trend for senior subordinated debentures; and</p>
<p>- Pfd-5 with a positive trend for series 1 and 2 senior preference shares.</p>
<p>At the end of 1995, Clyde had proved and probable reserves of 155 million barrels of oil equivalent, compared to Gulf's 793 million barrels.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
